    (v_test, 2, $q$NON_VERBAL$q$, 2, NULL, 16, $q$Codes$q$, $q$Three-letter codes$q$, $q$code$q$, $q$Each figure has a three-letter code. Work out what each letter stands for. What is the code for the last figure?$q$, $q$svg$q$, $q$<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 450 112" width="450" height="112"><g transform="translate(5,5)"><rect x="0" y="0" width="80" height="80" rx="6" fill="#ffffff" stroke="#9ca3af" stroke-width="1.5"/><circle cx="40" cy="40" r="30" fill="#ffffff" stroke="#1f2937" stroke-width="2"/><line x1="40.0" y1="30" x2="40.0" y2="50" stroke="#1f2937" stroke-width="2.5"/><circle cx="40" cy="18" r="3.5" fill="#1f2937"/></g><text x="45" y="104" font-size="16" font-weight="bold" text-anchor="middle" fill="#1f2937">APX</text><g transform="translate(95,5)"><rect x="0" y="0" width="80" height="80" rx="6" fill="#ffffff" stroke="#9ca3af" stroke-width="1.5"/><polygon points="61.2,18.8 61.2,61.2 18.8,61.2 18.8,18.8" fill="#ffffff" stroke="#1f2937" stroke-width="2"/><line x1="35.5" y1="30" x2="35.5" y2="50" stroke="#1f2937" stroke-width="2.5"/><line x1="44.5" y1="30" x2="44.5" y2="50" stroke="#1f2937" stroke-width="2.5"/><circle cx="40" cy="18" r="3.5" fill="#1f2937"/></g><text x="135" y="104" font-size="16" font-weight="bold" text-anchor="middle" fill="#1f2937">BQX</text><g transform="translate(185,5)"><rect x="0" y="0" width="80" height="80" rx="6" fill="#ffffff" stroke="#9ca3af" stroke-width="1.5"/><circle cx="40" cy="40" r="30" fill="#ffffff" stroke="#1f2937" stroke-width="2"/><line x1="31.0" y1="30" x2="31.0" y2="50" stroke="#1f2937" stroke-width="2.5"/><line x1="40.0" y1="30" x2="40.0" y2="50" stroke="#1f2937" stroke-width="2.5"/><line x1="49.0" y1="30" x2="49.0" y2="50" stroke="#1f2937" stroke-width="2.5"/><circle cx="40" cy="62" r="3.5" fill="#1f2937"/></g><text x="225" y="104" font-size="16" font-weight="bold" text-anchor="middle" fill="#1f2937">ARY</text><g transform="translate(275,5)"><rect x="0" y="0" width="80" height="80" rx="6" fil