    (v_test, 2, $q$NON_VERBAL$q$, 3, NULL, 19, $q$Folding$q$, $q$Fold over$q$, $q$paper folding$q$, $q$The paper is see-through. It is folded along the dashed line so that the left half lies on top of the right half. What does it look like?$q$, $q$svg$q$, $q$<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 90 90" width="90" height="90"><g transform="translate(5,5)"><rect x="0" y="0" width="80" height="80" rx="6" fill="#ffffff" stroke="#9ca3af" stroke-width="1.5"/><rect x="8" y="8" width="64" height="64" fill="#ffffff" stroke="#1f2937" stroke-width="2"/><line x1="40" y1="4" x2="40" y2="76" stroke="#1f2937" stroke-width="2" stroke-dasharray="5,4"/><rect x="12" y="14" width="12" height="12" fill="#1f2937"/><circle cx="30" cy="52" r="6" fill="#9ca3af" stroke="#1f2937" stroke-width="1.5"/><polygon points="14,64 26,64 14,44" fill="#ffffff" stroke="#1f2937" stroke-width="1.5"/></g></svg>$q$, $q$svg$q$, $q$<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 80 80" width="80" height="80"><rect x="40" y="8" width="32" height="64" fill="#e5e7eb" stroke="#1f2937" stroke-width="2"/><g transform="translate(0,80) scale(1,-1)"><g transform="translate(80,0) scale(-1,1)"><rect x="12" y="14" width="12" height="12" fill="#1f2937"/><circle cx="30" cy="52" r="6" fill="#9ca3af" stroke="#1f2937" stroke-width="1.5"/><polygon points="14,64 26,64 14,44" fill="#ffffff" stroke="#1f2937" stroke-width="1.5"/></g></g></svg>$q$, $q$<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 80 80" width="80" height="80"><rect x="40" y="8" width="32" height="64" fill="#e5e7eb" stroke="#1f2937" stroke-width="2"/><g transform="translate(80,0) scale(-1,1)"><rect x="12" y="14" width="12" height="12" fill="#1f2937"/><circle cx="30" cy="52" r="6" fill="#9ca3af" stroke="#1f2937" stroke-width="1.5"/><polygon points="14,64 26,64 14,44" fill="#ffffff" stroke="#1f2937" stroke-width="1.5"/></g></svg>$q$, $q$<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 80 80" width="80" height="80"><rect x="40" y="8" width="32" height="64" fill="#e5e7eb" stroke="#1f2937" stroke-width="2"/><g transform="translate(40,0)"><rect x="12" y="14" width="12" height="12" fill="#1f2937"/><circle cx="30" cy="52" r="6" fill="#9ca3af" stroke="#1f2937" stroke-width="1.5"/><polygon points="14,64 26,64 14,44" fill="#ffffff" stroke="#1f2937" stroke-width="1.5"/></g></svg>$q$, $q$<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 80 80" width="80" height="80"><rect x="40" y="8" width="32" height="64" fill="#e5e7eb" stroke="#1f2937" stroke-width="2"/><g transform="translate(80,0) scale(-1,1)"><rect x="12" y="14" width="12" height="12" fill="#1f2937"/><circle cx="30" cy="52" r="6" fill="#9ca3af" stroke="#1f2937" stroke-width="1.5"/></g></svg>$q$, $q$<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 80 80" width="80" height="80"><rect x="8" y="8" width="64" height="64" fill="#ffffff" stroke="#1f2937" stroke-width="2"/><line x1="40" y1="4" x2="40" y2="76" stroke="#1f2937" stroke-width="2" stroke-dasharray="5,4"/><rect x="12" y="14" width="12" height="12" fill="#1f2937"/><circle cx="30" cy="52" r="6" fill="#9ca3af" stroke="#1f2937" stroke-width="1.5"/><polygon points="14,64 26,64 14,44" fill="#ffffff" stroke="#1f2937" stroke-width="1.5"/><g transform="translate(80,0) scale(-1,1)"><rect x="12" y="14" width="12" height="12" fill="#1f2937"/><circle cx="30" cy="52" r="6" fill="#9ca3af" stroke="#1f2937" stroke-width="1.5"/><polygon points="14,64 26,64 14,44" fill="#ffffff" stroke="#1f2937" stroke-width="1.5"/></g></svg>$q$, $q$B$q$, $q$Folding over a line works like a mirror: each mark lands the same distance from the fold on the other side, so the pattern appears reflected on the right half.$q$),
